{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/683285-parent-advice-for-character-concept","id":683285,"title":"Parent advice for character concept","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-30T10:51:07-07:00","id":683285,"title":"Parent advice for character concept","content":"About to start playing a game with a new GM soon. She's forbidden Atlantis and the Yazatas, but nothing else (and I'm not familiar enough to check out fan material since I've been in two games before this).<br /> <br /> In a different game, I'm playing a Scion of Kali, so I don't want to be another Deva. I think Jotunblut's lame (and doesn't really fit the character concept), but all that means is that I don't have to worry about spending points in that purview. With those restrictions, what's everybody's first choice for:<br /> <br /> A bookish-but-durable scholar/student of Fate. His/her focused, indomitable spirit manifests physically, resulting in an unbreakable form (Epic Stamina, Guardian?). Their study of the cosmos reaches in the metaphysics of the world, and they have studied Magic thanks to their divine connection (Magic? Prophecy?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T16:43:30-07:00","id":683637,"title":"","content":"Durable mystic is a fairly common trope. I think Odin would work well, especially if you can talk your ST into using an alternate version of Jotunblut that isn't about creating (crappy) minions. Try <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/download/4g0oo59750osnet/Jotunblut.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a>, or <a href=\"http://www.thecbg.org/wiki/index.php?title=Jotunblut_%28Lost_Atlanta%29\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a>? Frigg is another Norse option.<br /> <br /> Hecate, over in the Dodekatheon, would be a good option... but she isn't canon and would require a fan write-up. Instead, maybe Athena, the Goddess of Wisdom and Tactics? <br /> <br /> There are the Eight Immortals who are <i>all about</i> some sturdy mysticism in China, but I can't think of any specific deities. <br /> <br /> As far as the Aztecs go, Xipe Totec might look favorably on someone super-resilient, but Tezcatlipoca would also be good for a bad-ass sorcerer. <br /> <br /> Kalfu might be a match for the Orishas, but I can't think off the top of my head of anyone from Japan that really fits. Egypt, of course, has Thoth, Ptah and Isis.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T18:20:52-07:00","id":691835,"title":"","content":"Might try Isis for a divine parent. She took down one of the most powerful gods through cunning and brought her husband back from the dead. Plus, she's a goddess of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T02:40:46-07:00","id":692170,"title":"","content":"Telgar and Nyrufa took many gods out of my mouth already. Still, I'll make a short list of gods I deem appropriate for this idea and why. Some will be re-iterations of what those two already said.<br /> <br /> Isis: Has Magic and Guardian, so two things that fit the bill. Also, Heku is pretty underestimated in my opinion and allows for your bookish scholar to use his knowledge of the Arcane and Names to an even bigger extend. Lore-wise, she isn't as book-ish as other gods but might support your character in his decision, as books keep him away from any dangerous thoughts. Nobody said Isis was a nice godparent.<br /> <br /> Thoth: Epic Intelligence, Magic and Heku make for some nice selling-points, but Moon and Justice may also be appealing for your concept. Also he is a bookworm himself, so you've got that going for him, as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Athena: Epic Intelligence and Epic Wits make for a good scholar, as does Arete. Sadly, she doesn't have anything else associated that would fit the bill. Still, lore-wise she would be a pretty solid parent for this character and have no qualms of getting him/her some good relics.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hephaestos: While there is only Epic Intelligence and Arete really speaking for him, I still wanted him included because I think he would support such a Scion by providing brilliant self-forged relics.<br /> <br /> Hermes: Again, Epic Intelligence and Arete make a pretty solid combo for your idea and there is Epic Wits and Magic to boost. Sure, he is a bit of a con-man, but who says that a bookish scholar can't be witty when the time calls for it?<br /> <br /> Frigg: Basically, Magic and Prophecy. If you don't like Jotunblut, check out the alternative versions Telgar provided or just leave it in the dust. Nobodys forcing you to take it.<br /> <br /> Odin: Has everything you want safe for Guardian. If I was your GM, though, I'd give you hell for choosing him, since he has so much stuff associated with him and his lore-text gives me the perfect excuse to do so. Just be warned.<br /> <br /> Huizilopochtli: Epic Stamina, Magic and Guardian are a good Combo. Also, Itzli provides you with Legend whenever you need it later on. Also I'd think the combination of a bad temper and a bookish personality would be hilarioius, but that might just be me.<br /> <br /> Tezcatlipoca: Pretty much the same as Odin. The List of things he doesn't have associated is longer than the list of things he has and Itzli, just like Huizilopochtli, fits your bill. Same as Odin though I'd personally give you hell for choosing him, but maybe your GM is a bit more forgiving on that.<br /> <br /> Quetzalcoatl: Lots. of. Purviews. Also, Epic Intelligence. And you can never go wrong with Itzli. Just be prepared for Tezcatlipoca Scions to burst your bubble of peace every now and again, but thats comes with the job.<br /> <br /> Raiden: He has Guardian, but thats pretty much it. The Amatsukami don't go much for things like that. Still, Tsukumo-Gami is way too useful to just overlook, especially if you want a scholar. Just ask the book what it knows.<br /> <br /> Omoikame: Not an official god, but if you can, maybe make her yourself: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omoikane_(Shinto\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omoikane_(Shinto</a>)<br /> <br /> Shango: You might be his ruling son. Prophecy, Sky and Epic Strength are nice and if you boost Epic Intelligence, Cheval becomes really, really nasty.<br /> <br /> Danu: She will support you, no matter what you do, and has Epic Stamina and Guardian. Enech could come in handy, too, especially Bard's Tongue, considering your concept. <br /> <br /> Lugh: Because he is Lugh. Pretty much any concept goes with him and his somehow supported, but you'd have to be a librarian who is also an Olympic-Level athlete and good-looking to boot to really come after your father. <br /> <br /> Fuxi: As the god of culture and refinement, he just goes with your concept, as do his Epic Intelligence and Epic Stamina. Plus, if you have a bit of imagination, you can use Taiyi to really spice things up. <br /> <br /> Xiwangmu: As an overseer of fate, she has many of the things you want and might even support your decision of becoming a scholar. If you wanna protect people, bear in mind that they have to be deserving, though. Chinese morals are a bit strange to us westeners, so I'd advise you to read up on them at least before playing this. <br /> <br /> Guan Yu/Huang Di: Both are guardians in a sense, so I took the liberty of bundling them together. They are both rulers, though, so make sure not to thread on their toes. <br /> <br /> Vishnu: As the preserver, he has an interest in collecting as much information as he can and so do you. He gives you Magic, Epic Intelligence and Guardian, plus the potentially game-breaking Samsara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8325,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","user":"Asmael","date":".  Added the last pantheons 10-07-2015, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T05:56:16-07:00","id":692309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/683285-parent-advice-for-character-concept?p=692170#post692170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isis: Has Magic and Guardian, so two things that fit the bill. Also, Heku is pretty underestimated in my opinion and allows for your bookish scholar to use his knowledge of the Arcane and Names to an even bigger extend. Lore-wise, she isn't as book-ish as other gods but might support your character in his decision, as books keep him away from any dangerous thoughts. Nobody said Isis was a nice godparent.<br /> <br /> Athena: Epic Intelligence and Epic Wits make for a good scholar, as does Arete. Sadly, she doesn't have anything else associated that would fit the bill. Still, lore-wise she would be a pretty solid parent for this character and have no qualms of getting him/her some good relics.<br /> <br /> Frigg: Basically, Magic and Prophecy. If you don't like Jotunblut, check out the alternative versions Telgar provided or just leave it in the dust. Nobodys forcing you to take it.<br /> <br /> Odin: Has everything you want safe for Guardian. If I was your GM, though, I'd give you hell for choosing him, since he has so much stuff associated with him and his lore-text gives me the perfect excuse to do so. Just be warned.<br /> <br /> Huizilopochtli: Epic Stamina, Magic and Guardian are a good Combo. Also, Itzli provides you with Legend whenever you need it later on. Also I'd think the combination of a bad temper and a bookish personality would be hilarioius, but that might just be me.<br /> <br /> Omoikame: Not an official god, but if you can, maybe make her yourself: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omoikane_(Shinto\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omoikane_(Shinto</a>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for Omoikane, I've been looking at those very gods for much the same reasons. Glad to know that I'm on the right page. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Omoikane looks good too, I'll run a version by my ST. Considering an alternate idea for the character is a dutiful, indomitable miko, it could work out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Time is running short, so I'll do the Tuatha, Celestial Bureaucracy and Deva later on. Bear with me. </div> </div> </div>Hey, I'm excited that you've helped so much already. Danke schoen!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T07:03:34-07:00","id":692430,"title":"","content":"Added the last ones in my post before, hopefully you find something that helps you. Especially the Deva have some other gods you might wanna read about, but those are the ones I think most befit your idea. Hopefully I was of some help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:58:46-07:00","id":692780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/683285-parent-advice-for-character-concept?p=692170#post692170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Athena: Epic Intelligence and Epic Wits make for a good scholar, as does Arete. Sadly, she doesn't have anything else associated that would fit the bill. Still, lore-wise she would be a pretty solid parent for this character and have no qualms of getting him/her some good relics.<br /> <br /> <br /> Odin: Has everything you want safe for Guardian. If I was your GM, though, I'd give you hell for choosing him, since he has so much stuff associated with him and his lore-text gives me the perfect excuse to do so. Just be warned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, isn't Athena the goddess of strategic combat? That would suit perfectly for somebody who's not the hack and slash type of fighter.<br /> <br /> Odin, if I'm not mistaken either hung or crucified himself from the world tree for 9 days and plucked out an eye just to obtain omniscience.<br /> <br /> The Chinese pantheon's PSP apparently has a strong focus in alchemy and transition from one state to another. For a scholar of Fate and such, that could be very suiting. In fact, one of its god level abilities lets you turn people immortal or even completely rewrite their characters.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T13:04:03-07:00","id":692863,"title":"","content":"Athena is the goddess of strategic combat, but also of wisdom, the Fine Arts and Artisanry. <br /> <br /> Odin crucified himself to Yggdrassil for nine days until he died and was magically resurrected, you're right on that count. However, he either did this to become even wiser by mastering death or to gain the knowledge of runes, sources differ there. He also didn't pluck out his eye to gain omniscience (which was given to him by sitting on his throne Hli\u00f0skj\u00e1lf), but to gain the gift of divination. The eye was the price the giant Mimir took from him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T13:44:07-07:00","id":692879,"title":"","content":"I&quot;d like to add Chiron to this grouping. The son of Cronus and Philyra (an Oceanid). He's Zeus' half brother and the teacher of many heroes and demigods. <br /> <br /> A great healer, astrologer, and respected oracle, Chiron was highly revered as a teacher and tutor. Among his pupils were many culture heroes: Asclepius,Aristaeus, Ajax, Aeneas, Actaeon, Caeneus, Theseus, Achilles, Jason, Peleus, Telamon, Perseus, sometimes Heracles, Oileus, Phoenix, and in one Byzantine tradition, even Dionysus: according to Ptolemaeus Chennus of Alexandria, &quot;Dionysus was loved by Chiron, from whom he learned chants and dances, the bacchic rites and initiations.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T06:22:39-07:00","id":693807,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the help everybody. I decided to go with Xiwangdu. Taiyi is pretty cool, and Xiwangdu has Epic Stamina, Magic, and Health. I hadn't looked at the Celestial Bureaucracy at all before this, so I'm glad y'all put me on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T08:38:22-07:00","id":693883,"title":"","content":"You're welcome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T22:11:05-08:00","id":783934,"title":"","content":"I know I'm late, so this is only worth stating for future characters in the hopes that it helps.<br /> <br /> But it is totally possible to have a character with access to a purview not associated with your divine parent. It costs a little extra in bonus points, I think, at character creation, but as long as you clear it with ST, there's no reason your character shouldn't have a relic which gives them access to a purview normally associated with another god. As long as you can come up with a valid reason for them to have it, that is.<br /> <br /> For example, in one of my campaigns, I had a player ask me if their scion of Athena could have a relic granting her access to the Magic purview. I told him to come up with a good enough backstory and I'd consider it. What we came up with: Since all of Athena's scions are adopted, it was decided that Athena asked Hermes for the right to adopt one of his sirelings. He accepted, on the condition that she grant the child one birthright she wouldn't necessarily approve of. It turned out to be a harp that granted the Magic purview among other things, and turned out to be a pretty funny character point, since the character had no musical ability to speak of, but had to play the harp to access her magic, which she did fairly often.<br /> <br /> Long story short, you can always work out with your ST how to get a purview for a character who otherwise perfectly fits another parent.<br /> Hope that was helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10163-toomuchjesus","name":"Toomuchjesus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:28:54-08:00","id":796952,"title":"","content":"About Jotunblut, yes, it is the Pantheon-specific purview that everybody seems to agree to dislike, but it ain't completely useless if the player is up to toying with buffing minions and doing some inane stuff, like an adventurous jackass of a scion of Hel who liked to play &quot;vampire master&quot; to the group of goth and biker girls he turned in his &quot;slayer brides&quot; berserker band/gang. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As he soon found out, berserkers make even more difficult lovers than soldiers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-30-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T12:56:30-08:00","id":797470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/683285-parent-advice-for-character-concept?p=796952#post796952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Jotunblut, yes, it is the Pantheon-specific purview that everybody seems to agree to dislike, but it ain't completely useless if the player is up to toying with buffing minions and doing some inane stuff, like an adventurous jackass of a scion of Hel who liked to play &quot;vampire master&quot; to the group of goth and biker girls he turned in his &quot;slayer brides&quot; berserker band/gang. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As he soon found out, berserkers make even more difficult lovers than soldiers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Excuse me? How can you possibly dislike a perview that turns people into viking berserkers!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T14:18:38-08:00","id":797507,"title":"","content":"Because it does a terrible job of that. The berserkers are pathetic past Legend 2. Jotunblut minions are just... lame. They're never going to keep up with a Demigod or God, and most of the time they can't even keep up with a Hero. Plus, it has no benefit <i>for you</i>, meaning it <i>only</i> provides use for characters interested in building a team of minions. That's awfully restrictive to be a PSP for every single Norse character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T16:41:35-08:00","id":797552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/683285-parent-advice-for-character-concept?p=797507#post797507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it does a terrible job of that. The berserkers are pathetic past Legend 2. Jotunblut minions are just... lame. They're never going to keep up with a Demigod or God, and most of the time they can't even keep up with a Hero. Plus, it has no benefit <i>for you</i>, meaning it <i>only</i> provides use for characters interested in building a team of minions. That's awfully restrictive to be a PSP for every single Norse character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You could say the same about all minions, given their limited capacity to advance. Unless you're taking on fellow Scions or even the Titans themselves, they sound like they should be useful tools to aid in the situation. Heck a god level Jotunblut actually lets you turn people into Giants.Also, you're usually not carrying just one or two minions. You're carrying whole groups with you, so they have the advantage of numbers. Kane Taoka had 15 Shinobi he could whip out at a moment's notice. Icarus had like 10+ Minotaur somehow.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think the Minions were supposed to be used as a resource, not a weapon. Legends don't say &quot;And thus the hero of the story hid behind a wall of soldiers who dispatched the evil monster.&quot; They say the hero lead the charge from the front lines, while his troops helped to corner the beast.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Hero book says that a squad of trained Mercenaries poses a threat to a Hero, and they're just base humans with military training. Now imagine a squad of mercenaries hopped up on Jotunblut with access to epic strength / stamina. Plus, the more advanced your Jotunblut level is, the stronger the benefits they receive, so the minions will grow more powerful over time. Provided you focus on increasing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-31-2015, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T17:55:52-08:00","id":797570,"title":"","content":"But once you hit Demigod, the benefits don't scale up enough. Your Jotunblut minions can't <i>do</i> anything. They can't corner the beast, because the beast will eat them, all of them, in one bite. The best they can do is be your servants for social reasons. That isn't worth a PSP. It's just a terribly weak PSP compared to every other one written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:40:13-08:00","id":797803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/683285-parent-advice-for-character-concept?p=797570#post797570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But once you hit Demigod, the benefits don't scale up enough. Your Jotunblut minions can't <i>do</i> anything. They can't corner the beast, because the beast will eat them, all of them, in one bite. The best they can do is be your servants for social reasons. That isn't worth a PSP. It's just a terribly weak PSP compared to every other one written.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> True. But as far as I'm aware, there's no real limit to how many minions you can have as long as you keep buying them. And once you achieve Demigod / God, you encounter minions worthy of somebody holding that station. Now true, building an entire army of minions may not seem interesting at first, but if you're going for a War God style of character, then it makes more sense. By the time you become a God, you've probably got an entire regiment marching behind you to battle the Titanspawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T08:05:24-08:00","id":797818,"title":"","content":"Right. That's useful for a <i>very</i> specific type of character. It's foolish for that to be the <i>entire</i> focus of the Norse, when almost <i>none</i> of them even have a mythology as troop-leaders. They're all solo shows, or at <i>best</i> one or two sidekicks, like Thor's son or Freyr's sword-bearer. Jotunblut is a terrible fit for their mythology, it's utter weaksauce compared to any other PSP, and it's only even useful for a handful of concepts. So, yeah, it's not a surprise that it's generally given a bunch of shit. It's shitty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T17:26:52-08:00","id":798502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/683285-parent-advice-for-character-concept?p=797818#post797818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. That's useful for a <i>very</i> specific type of character. It's foolish for that to be the <i>entire</i> focus of the Norse, when almost <i>none</i> of them even have a mythology as troop-leaders. They're all solo shows, or at <i>best</i> one or two sidekicks, like Thor's son or Freyr's sword-bearer. Jotunblut is a terrible fit for their mythology, it's utter weaksauce compared to any other PSP, and it's only even useful for a handful of concepts. So, yeah, it's not a surprise that it's generally given a bunch of shit. It's shitty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Won't disagree with you on that, specially considering that part of what lead to make the Scion of Hel was to make fun of Jotunblut and the Aesir in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It might be made more efficient with some new powers and expansions, but then what you would have is some monster-maker like Scion's version of Ixion, that has nothing whatsoever to do with norse imagery or mythos. Personally, i always felt that something building up from Prophecy or Fate-Binding might be far more interesting and appropriate as a PSP for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T22:57:58-08:00","id":799074,"title":"","content":"I think one of the problems regarding minions is the game itself was actually designed to give Scions the advantage. Heck, the Hero book advises story tellers that the Scions are actually supposed to win confrontations and overcome challenges. Your job as the ST is to make the story grand and legendary, not to party wipe the whole Band.<br /> <br /> This sounds good in a PvE style of gaming, but when you've got player vs player, I can see how minions would be more of a liability than helpful. At that point, you're better off just hurling buildings or conjuring fireballs to win a battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T00:54:06-08:00","id":799154,"title":"","content":"Just check out Demigod-Level Enemies. Just do it. And then take the average Berserker or Einherjar, give them the highest iteration of Jotunblut possible at this stage and simulate a few battles. It won't end well. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of Jotunblut in theory, but practically it just doesn't cut it. The Greeks can pretty much wipe the floor with most enemies if they have battle-centered Arete, the Atzlanti basically have free Legend and the Amatsukami can excel almost as much as the Greeks at certain tasks and talk to things to boot. Heck, even the Loa can at some point just go around and absorb Titanspawns to take over their abilities or just make them jump off a cliff or worse. Even the scrambled Heku-Purview can be used for much more efficient results than Jotunblut. Just for fun, let's see what the PSP do on Level 10: <br /> <br /> Arete: Forty-Six bonus dice (that's 46), or twenty-three potential rerolls on an ability you have maxed out. That's about 20 successes and I'm being generous here. And let's not forget that Arete isn't limited to one ability, but you could have it on as many abilities as you want. <br /> Cheval: Allows you to use each and all Cheval-Boons on Titanspawn. You can see through their eyes. You can hear their thoughts. You can control them to fight in your stead. You could absorb them to gain some of their better abilities. <br /> Heku: After quite some time, you can basically control somebody. It's like Overt Order, but better, longer-lasting and not subject to interpretation. <br /> Itztli: You get additional Legend for killing someone from your family. It's a dear sacrifice, alright, but assuming you just have a bunch of throwaway Hero-Scions, that's +50 total Legend Points for free. And even more if you can get a Demigod- or even God-Level Scion to die for you. Oh, and it fills up that pool, too. <br /> Jotunblut: Can reverse the effect of a Mortal having drunk the blood of a Giant. <br /> Tsukumo-Gami: Can transfer Kamis from Object to Object, effectively creating or destroying relics. <br /> <br /> It might seem that I'm nitpicking here, but believe me: Jotunblut loses this contest on every level of the ladder in the long run. It might seem viable on Hero at first, but if you go ahead and take a far-off look into the future that is Demigod and finally God, even that loses its appeal very quickly. Telgar is right: Jotunblut sucks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T05:11:40-08:00","id":799537,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think Arete adds OP to something that was already OP to begin with. Epic Attributes give automatic successes. At level 10, these are about 46 successes, which means you may as well not even roll at that point. Then you have Arete which allows you to add even more dice on top of that. I get it, the Greeks embodied perfection in everything and their gods were capable of amazing shit. But I only have <b>two</b> 8 sided dice in my possession and I can't spend 5 minutes rolling over 100 dice every time I take an action. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-03-2016, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T09:30:48-08:00","id":799669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/683285-parent-advice-for-character-concept?p=799537#post799537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think Arete adds OP to something that was already OP to begin with. Epic Attributes give automatic successes. At level 10, these are about 46 successes, which means you may as well not even roll at that point. Then you have Arete which allows you to add even more dice on top of that. I get it, the Greeks embodied perfection in everything and their gods were capable of amazing shit. But I only have two 8 sided dice in my possession and I can't spend 5 minutes rolling over 100 dice every time I take an action. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it can sort of turn a session of Scion into a Dragon Ball game at demigod level or higher. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T10:23:12-08:00","id":799690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/683285-parent-advice-for-character-concept?p=799669#post799669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it can sort of turn a session of Scion into a Dragon Ball game at demigod level or higher. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thing is, as horrendously broken as the game mechanics become later down the line, the game itself offers some great writing material. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T10:53:04-08:00","id":799702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/683285-parent-advice-for-character-concept?p=799690#post799690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Thing is, as horrendously broken as the game mechanics become later down the line, the game itself offers some great writing material. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Must admit i'm quite curious about how the Sardonyx system will deal with these and other issues in its completed form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}